 "instructions": "# Task (tuition round): official international tuition fees for entities whose programmes have no fee yet\n\nFor every item in \"tasks\" (an institution; \"empty_programmes\" = how many of its bachelor/master programmes still lack a fee; \"sample\" = example programme names) find the OFFICIAL annual tuition fee for INTERNATIONAL (non-EU / non-home) students, from the institution's own website.\n\nWhere to look: \"Tuition and fees\", \"Fees and costs\", \"Cost of attendance\", \"International students > fees\", fee tables, and fee schedules published as PDF or spreadsheet on the school's own site. On selector pages (country / programme / level) choose Turkey or \"international / non-EU\". Expand accordions and tabs; read hidden text.\nRules: official domains only (no agents, aggregators, forums); browse at human pace; if a page asks you to solve a CAPTCHA or blocks automated access, do not try to get around it: record page_status \"blocked\" and the URL in manual_check_url and go on with other official pages. Never guess or estimate. Latest published academic year; state the year.\n\nResult per institution: one object with a \"fees\" list (one entry per fee band / programme group that the school publishes; use the school's own grouping, e.g. by faculty, subject band, level, or per programme):\n{\"entity\": \"<same name as in the task>\", \"country\": \"...\",\n \"page_status\": \"read | blocked | not_found | js_empty\", \"confidence\": \"high | medium | low\",\n \"source_urls\": [\"exact pages or PDFs read\"], \"manual_check_url\": null,\n \"fees\": [ {\"level\": \"bachelor | master\", \"applies_to\": \"who this fee covers, e.g. 'all undergraduate', 'Engineering and Computer Science', 'MBA', or an exact programme name\",\n            \"amount_per_year\": 0, \"currency\": \"GBP|USD|EUR|CAD|AUD|...\", \"academic_year\": \"2026/27\",\n            \"period_note\": \"per year / per credit / total programme / per semester (as the school states it)\" } ],\n \"note\": \"short factual remark (what is excluded, e.g. lab fees; fees only for some campuses)\"}\n\nIf the school publishes only per-credit or total-programme prices, record them with the school's unit in period_note; do not convert.\n\nSubmit: POST https://paneledu.com/api/agent/results with header X-Agent-Token: <token you were given>, Content-Type: application/json, body = JSON list of result objects (a few per request, each as soon as done). The field \"school\" is required by the server: set it to the entity name too. Expected answer: {\"ok\":true,\"saved\":N}.\n",
